         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/abb55480-4a35-4dc3-b0c1-02f8fc99054a,1794693661471/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C535%2C5712%2C3213%29%3B' alt='Some members of the Holy Name of Mary College choir. Eight women stand together in a classroom wearing blue choir T-shirts.' width='620' height='349' title='Some members of the Holy Name of Mary College choir made up of the high school&apos;s alumnae. The Mississauga school shut its doors in June and now the six-decade-old building&apos;s future is up in the air. Hundreds of former staff and students gathered on Saturday for a final mass to say goodbye to the school.'/><p>Hundreds of alumnae and staff gathered on Saturday for a final mass to farewell their former Catholic high school building, which is facing an uncertain future. The Holy Name of Mary College School in Mississauga closed in June due to low enrolment. Its owners, the Felician Sisters of St. Francis, are deciding what to do with the 62 year-old building.</p>]]></description>
